854
00:24:01,360 --> 00:24:03,360
I'm pretty passive by nature.

855
00:24:03,360 --> 00:24:03,880
Yeah.

856
00:24:05,520 --> 00:24:07,520
I was a little stunned when I saw him.

857
00:24:08,200 --> 00:24:09,240
You really didn't expect it.

858
00:24:10,120 --> 00:24:11,360
Yeah.

859
00:24:16,270 --> 00:24:17,000
Then let's go.

860
00:24:17,460 --> 00:24:17,860
Let's go.

861
00:24:18,660 --> 00:24:20,780
(Happy)

862
00:24:21,530 --> 00:24:22,680
Yours smells really good.

863
00:24:22,940 --> 00:24:23,780
(Happy)

864
00:24:23,780 --> 00:24:24,880
Smell this.

865
00:24:28,650 --> 00:24:29,760
I'll take off my jacket.

866
00:24:29,760 --> 00:24:30,610
Honestly.

867
00:24:32,920 --> 00:24:34,200
He's sweating like crazy.

868
00:24:34,200 --> 00:24:36,280
I could tell he was pretty nervous.

869
00:24:37,410 --> 00:24:39,200
Courage is something

870
00:24:39,200 --> 00:24:41,200
I really lack.

871
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:43,180
But you were pretty brave yesterday.

872
00:24:43,470 --> 00:24:45,120
That moment you knocked on the door.

873
00:24:45,600 --> 00:24:46,900
That took a lot of courage.

874
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:50,190
Thanks.

875
00:24:53,470 --> 00:24:55,730
That's the Courageous' flower?

876
00:24:57,110 --> 00:24:58,990
It's a flower the Courageous gave you.

877
00:24:58,990 --> 00:25:02,500
(The flower for you)

878
00:25:02,520 --> 00:25:03,680
Very good at talking.

879
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:09,080
I've never seen this side of Zhao Xilun.

880
00:25:09,480 --> 00:25:10,840
This is the first time.

881
00:25:10,840 --> 00:25:11,920
He gets so nervous

882
00:25:13,080 --> 00:25:13,840
around you.

883
00:25:13,840 --> 00:25:14,920
I've never seen him this nervous.

884
00:25:14,920 --> 00:25:15,920
He actually talks less.

885
00:25:15,920 --> 00:25:17,640
Yeah, I feel like he does talk less.

886
00:25:18,160 --> 00:25:18,640
I remember now.

887
00:25:18,640 --> 00:25:20,680
At first, I thought
he only saw me as a friend

888
00:25:20,680 --> 00:25:21,440
because I noticed

889
00:25:21,440 --> 00:25:22,760
he could talk

890
00:25:23,200 --> 00:25:23,720
to every other girl,

891
00:25:23,720 --> 00:25:24,880
but he wouldn't talk to me.

892
00:25:25,620 --> 00:25:26,520
He's only like that with girls he likes.

893
00:25:26,520 --> 00:25:27,840
I thought he had something against me.

894
00:25:29,200 --> 00:25:29,920
It was a misunderstanding.

895
00:25:32,520 --> 00:25:33,290
It's done.

896
00:25:33,570 --> 00:25:34,230
It's fixed.

897
00:25:34,230 --> 00:25:35,240
You're really good at this.

898
00:25:35,930 --> 00:25:36,920
You're really good.

899
00:25:38,510 --> 00:25:39,070
He's happy.

900
00:25:39,890 --> 00:25:40,600
What now?

901
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:46,130
What else can we do?

902
00:25:48,550 --> 00:25:49,390
He's flustered.

903
00:25:50,140 --> 00:25:50,850
What should we do?

904
00:25:51,080 --> 00:25:51,890
Add something to it.

905
00:25:51,890 --> 00:25:52,500
Right.

906
00:25:52,750 --> 00:25:53,860
I was just...

907
00:25:54,640 --> 00:25:55,640
Yeah.

908
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:57,350
No.

909
00:26:05,960 --> 00:26:07,760
Let me explain this one.

910
00:26:09,960 --> 00:26:11,440
When the teaser came out,

911
00:26:11,440 --> 00:26:14,000
one of my female friends told me

912
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:15,400
that whenever I laugh,

913
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:16,560
I tend to touch people.

914
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:18,160
I didn't know why she said that,

915
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:19,160
but seeing this scene

916
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:21,000
reminded me of it.

917
00:26:21,600 --> 00:26:23,200
I guess I really didn't

918
00:26:23,440 --> 00:26:25,440
pay much attention to it.

919
00:26:26,480 --> 00:26:27,960
It's not a big deal.

920
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:29,480
I actually like doing that too.

921
00:26:29,480 --> 00:26:30,760
Touching someone when I laugh.

922
00:26:31,280 --> 00:26:32,440
It's just instinctive.

923
00:26:32,440 --> 00:26:33,120
Instinctive.

924
00:26:33,120 --> 00:26:34,640
Yeah.

925
00:26:34,640 --> 00:26:36,250
We're pretty funny together.

926
00:26:37,460 --> 00:26:38,680
We're really something.

927
00:26:41,370 --> 00:26:42,180
What should we eat later?

928
00:26:45,890 --> 00:26:47,050
Actually...

929
00:26:47,050 --> 00:26:48,100
Do you have plans?

930
00:26:52,570 --> 00:26:53,280
Maybe next time.

931
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:54,320
Oh right.

932
00:26:54,320 --> 00:26:55,480
Zhao Xilun told me that.

933
00:26:55,760 --> 00:26:57,560
He said that when he and Sha Yue'er

934
00:26:57,560 --> 00:26:59,240
were doing crafts,

935
00:26:59,240 --> 00:27:00,440
Sha Yue'er kept asking

936
00:27:00,440 --> 00:27:01,640
what they were going to eat later.

937
00:27:01,780 --> 00:27:02,280
I was hungry.

938
00:27:02,280 --> 00:27:04,040
Yeah.

939
00:27:04,040 --> 00:27:07,400
He said that on the day of your date,

940
00:27:07,400 --> 00:27:08,960
he felt a little awkward

941
00:27:08,960 --> 00:27:10,960
and wasn't very happy with how he acted.

942
00:27:11,240 --> 00:27:12,760
He actually did really well.

943
00:27:12,760 --> 00:27:16,640
Did your impression of Zhao Xilun
change after that?

944
00:27:17,360 --> 00:27:18,680
Honestly,

945
00:27:19,560 --> 00:27:22,920
not by much.

946
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:25,560
I just felt like we really clicked.

947
00:27:25,560 --> 00:27:26,360
Because in my everyday life,

948
00:27:26,760 --> 00:27:28,040
I rarely have

949
00:27:28,040 --> 00:27:30,920
such deep conversations with guys.

950
00:27:30,920 --> 00:27:33,160
And he's actually the person

951
00:27:33,160 --> 00:27:35,880
I've opened up to the fastest in years.

952
00:27:35,880 --> 00:27:38,720
So I didn't even realize
I'd start thinking...

953
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:39,680
You didn't know
what you were feeling either.

954
00:27:39,680 --> 00:27:40,880
Yeah, exactly.

955
00:27:41,400 --> 00:27:43,600
So, Chen Hewen,
after you watched their date,

956
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:44,880
did you feel a little regretful?

957
00:27:44,880 --> 00:27:47,840
Regret not getting The Courageous?

958
00:27:47,840 --> 00:27:49,920
Honestly, I was a little bummed.

959
00:28:01,320 --> 00:28:02,920
Everyone's out on dates.

960
00:28:03,650 --> 00:28:04,130
Hello.

961
00:28:04,720 --> 00:28:05,560
Hey, that's me.

962
00:28:06,900 --> 00:28:07,430
Hi.

963
00:28:07,430 --> 00:28:08,080
Pretty.

964
00:28:08,080 --> 00:28:08,510
Hello.

965
00:28:08,510 --> 00:28:09,330
So it's the five of us.

966
00:28:09,330 --> 00:28:09,970
Yeah.

967
00:28:13,590 --> 00:28:14,910
I think I had the heat

968
00:28:14,910 --> 00:28:15,600
up too high.

969
00:28:15,600 --> 00:28:16,360
It's kinda burnt.

970
00:28:17,890 --> 00:28:19,200
It's already black.

971
00:28:19,500 --> 00:28:21,540
(Totally burnt)

972
00:28:21,760 --> 00:28:23,760
Too much heat.
I have zero cooking talent.

973
00:28:23,760 --> 00:28:24,330
Okay.

974
00:28:25,050 --> 00:28:25,920
Let me try

975
00:28:25,920 --> 00:28:26,730
my potato slices.

976
00:28:29,550 --> 00:28:30,720
Looks like they're not great.

977
00:28:35,100 --> 00:28:36,500
So we're the odd-numbered group.

978
00:28:36,950 --> 00:28:37,360
Yeah.

979
00:28:37,900 --> 00:28:39,320
So are the three of them together?

980
00:28:39,950 --> 00:28:41,600
I guess he'll be with her for this slot,

981
00:28:41,600 --> 00:28:42,230
and then the next slot...

982
00:28:42,230 --> 00:28:43,030
I think.

983
00:28:43,030 --> 00:28:43,510
When time's up,

984
00:28:43,510 --> 00:28:44,320
he'll just leave.

985
00:28:44,630 --> 00:28:45,760
Time's up, you leave.

986
00:28:46,180 --> 00:28:47,650
But if it's all just today,

987
00:28:47,650 --> 00:28:48,540
that sounds really rushed.

988
00:28:48,540 --> 00:28:49,280
Feels like these guys

989
00:28:49,280 --> 00:28:50,880
already planned their whole day out.

990
00:28:50,880 --> 00:28:51,370
Yeah.

991
00:28:51,370 --> 00:28:52,330
I think for us,

992
00:28:52,330 --> 00:28:52,730
comparatively,

993
00:28:52,730 --> 00:28:54,100
it's a lot more relaxed.

994
00:28:54,720 --> 00:28:55,840
Were you really relaxed?

995
00:28:55,920 --> 00:28:58,100
I was okay, actually.

996
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:01,440
Honestly, that day was pretty nice.

997
00:29:01,440 --> 00:29:02,680
Our five-person date

998
00:29:02,680 --> 00:29:03,600
was pretty harmonious.

999
00:29:03,600 --> 00:29:04,440
It was really chill.

1000
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:05,240
A really chill...

1001
00:29:05,240 --> 00:29:05,720
Vibe.

1002
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:06,200
Yeah.

1003
00:29:07,480 --> 00:29:10,480
One of my happiest moments
in my first few days here

1004
00:29:10,480 --> 00:29:12,120
was that five-person date.

1005
00:29:12,520 --> 00:29:15,160
I was really happy that day
because Si and I

1006
00:29:15,160 --> 00:29:16,480
got to know each other better.

1007
00:29:16,480 --> 00:29:17,560
(Got to know each other better)

1008
00:29:17,560 --> 00:29:18,600
Before that,

1009
00:29:18,600 --> 00:29:19,760
I didn't really know Si.

1010
00:29:20,040 --> 00:29:21,600
She didn't talk much either.

1011
00:29:21,600 --> 00:29:23,200
Then when she got out of the car,

1012
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:24,600
she casually called out,

1013
00:29:24,600 --> 00:29:25,000
"Sun Bohan".

1014
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:26,000
It just felt really...

1015
00:29:26,960 --> 00:29:27,560
I was really happy.

1016
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:29,400
It was the first time
she'd said my name.

1017
00:29:31,480 --> 00:29:32,360
Yeah.

1018
00:29:34,720 --> 00:29:36,320
I'll grab the camera.

1019
00:29:37,520 --> 00:29:38,560
Chen Hewen, let's go together.

1020
00:29:39,840 --> 00:29:40,800
The moon tonight

1021
00:29:40,800 --> 00:29:41,520
is pretty big.

1022
00:29:41,520 --> 00:29:42,150
Yeah.

1023
00:29:44,860 --> 00:29:45,660
(Backing up)

1024
00:29:45,660 --> 00:29:46,370
Backing up.

1025
00:29:46,580 --> 00:29:47,580
Back.

1026
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:50,160
Why didn't you bring Si along?

1027
00:29:50,160 --> 00:29:52,240
Yeah, she was all by herself.

1028
00:29:52,880 --> 00:29:54,560
I didn't think that much about it.

1029
00:29:54,560 --> 00:29:56,120
Even though it was a five-person date,

1030
00:29:56,120 --> 00:29:58,480
it was really more
like two separate dates.

1031
00:29:58,480 --> 00:30:00,720
Yu Yang and Liang Renfang sat on the left,

1032
00:30:00,720 --> 00:30:01,760
and the three of us sat on the right.

1033
00:30:01,760 --> 00:30:02,480
They had their group.

1034
00:30:02,480 --> 00:30:03,320
And you had yours.

1035
00:30:03,320 --> 00:30:05,720
Yeah. When the two of them were talking,

1036
00:30:05,720 --> 00:30:07,560
the three of us kept our distance

1037
00:30:07,560 --> 00:30:09,400
to give them some privacy.

1038
00:30:12,290 --> 00:30:13,360
I really wanna hear

1039
00:30:13,360 --> 00:30:14,210
Si say something to me

1040
00:30:14,210 --> 00:30:15,760
in a real Northeastern accent.

1041
00:30:16,100 --> 00:30:17,740
(Excited)

1042
00:30:21,720 --> 00:30:22,700
(Demonstrates first)
What're you doing?

1043
00:30:22,800 --> 00:30:24,040
Sorry.

1044
00:30:24,040 --> 00:30:25,010
I was a little embarrassed.

1045
00:30:25,010 --> 00:30:25,660
So shy.

1046
00:30:26,290 --> 00:30:26,950
Si,

1047
00:30:26,950 --> 00:30:27,540
whatcha doin'?

1048
00:30:27,540 --> 00:30:28,030
Wassup?

1049
00:30:28,120 --> 00:30:29,320
(Is that how you say it?)
Si's so cute.

1050
00:30:29,470 --> 00:30:30,220
What's up?

1051
00:30:30,370 --> 00:30:31,110
Whatcha doin'?

1052
00:30:31,110 --> 00:30:32,110
Whatcha doin', Si?

1053
00:30:34,040 --> 00:30:35,120
You even demonstrated it for her.

1054
00:30:35,120 --> 00:30:37,240
Yeah, Si wasn't talking much then,

1055
00:30:37,240 --> 00:30:38,600
and she was sitting in the back.

1056
00:30:38,600 --> 00:30:39,960
So you were trying to get her involved?

1057
00:30:39,960 --> 00:30:40,560
Yeah.

1058
00:30:40,560 --> 00:30:43,760
I wanted her to open up a bit more.

1059
00:30:43,760 --> 00:30:45,520
Yeah. I think that was

1060
00:30:45,520 --> 00:30:46,880
one of my happiest days here.

1061
00:30:48,560 --> 00:30:50,880
I really was grateful
to both of them that day.

1062
00:30:51,560 --> 00:30:53,320
Even when you ate my raw potato slices,

1063
00:30:53,320 --> 00:30:54,480
you still felt that way?

1064
00:30:55,080 --> 00:30:55,880
They were actually really good.

1065
00:30:55,880 --> 00:30:57,120
I can still remember the taste.

1066
00:30:57,920 --> 00:31:00,760
I didn't really know Chen Hewen
or Sun Bohan that well

1067
00:31:00,760 --> 00:31:01,480
back then.

1068
00:31:01,480 --> 00:31:03,080
Yeah, but as we spent time together,

1069
00:31:03,080 --> 00:31:04,840
I later told Sun Bohan

1070
00:31:04,840 --> 00:31:06,160
that it felt really warm.

1071
00:31:06,160 --> 00:31:08,120
Almost like being with family.

1072
00:31:08,120 --> 00:31:09,920
That's really how it felt

1073
00:31:09,920 --> 00:31:10,800
when we were together.

1074
00:31:10,800 --> 00:31:12,280
I even told you both in the car.

1075
00:31:12,280 --> 00:31:13,560
I really appreciated that day.

1076
00:31:13,840 --> 00:31:15,400
Friends need
to encourage each other too.

1077
00:31:16,880 --> 00:31:18,760
Since we're friends around the same age,

1078
00:31:18,760 --> 00:31:21,720
I wanted to create a space

1079
00:31:21,720 --> 00:31:22,920
where you could

1080
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:25,360
open up a little more.

1081
00:31:25,360 --> 00:31:26,560
So you could talk to us more...

1082
00:31:28,440 --> 00:31:29,520
What is it?

1083
00:31:30,040 --> 00:31:31,200
Don't cry.

1084
00:31:31,800 --> 00:31:33,480
You're touched, huh?

1085
00:31:33,480 --> 00:31:34,280
Yeah.

1086
00:31:34,640 --> 00:31:36,880
I never got the chance
to tell you guys afterward.

1087
00:31:36,880 --> 00:31:38,320
I really appreciated that day.

1088
00:31:44,640 --> 00:31:45,480
Earlier in the house,

1089
00:31:45,480 --> 00:31:46,720
I barely talked.

1090
00:31:46,720 --> 00:31:47,880
But those two

1091
00:31:47,880 --> 00:31:50,080
really looked out for me that day.

1092
00:31:50,720 --> 00:31:52,120
They're both really thoughtful guys.

1093
00:31:52,120 --> 00:31:52,640
Yeah.

1094
00:31:57,200 --> 00:31:58,800
I think Sun Bohan's about to cry too.

1095
00:32:01,040 --> 00:32:02,400
Don't cry.

1096
00:32:02,400 --> 00:32:03,920
I can't handle seeing girls cry.

1097
00:32:03,920 --> 00:32:05,040
When I see a girl cry, I get...

1098
00:32:05,440 --> 00:32:07,240
You're both really emotional people.

1099
00:32:08,600 --> 00:32:10,000
I actually thought he was pretty aloof.

1100
00:32:10,060 --> 00:32:11,080
(Aloof)

1101
00:32:11,080 --> 00:32:13,400
But then I realized he's
nothing like that.

1102
00:32:13,400 --> 00:32:14,320
It's a total contrast.

1103
00:32:14,320 --> 00:32:15,040
(Unexpected contrast)
A contrast.

1104
00:32:15,040 --> 00:32:16,240
Yeah, I'm kinda slow.

1105
00:32:16,240 --> 00:32:17,240
(Slow and goofy)
I'm more of a goofy kind of guy.

1106
00:32:17,240 --> 00:32:18,880
Yeah, but you're smart.

1107
00:32:18,880 --> 00:32:19,420
(Smart)

1108
00:32:19,420 --> 00:32:20,060
I'm not.

1109
00:32:20,060 --> 00:32:21,000
(Really not)
I'm really not smart.

1110
00:32:21,320 --> 00:32:22,660
(Smart)
You are.

1111
00:32:23,360 --> 00:32:24,320
I'm honestly pretty dumb.

1112
00:32:24,320 --> 00:32:25,760
I'm nowhere near as smart as Zhao Xilun.

1113
00:32:25,760 --> 00:32:26,680
He really is smart.

1114
00:32:28,640 --> 00:32:31,440
I felt like everyone
really opened up in the car.

1115
00:32:31,440 --> 00:32:33,040
Especially when it was just
the three of us.

1116
00:32:33,040 --> 00:32:34,680
The two of them suddenly

1117
00:32:34,680 --> 00:32:36,320
made me feel like there

1118
00:32:36,320 --> 00:32:37,640
wasn't that same feeling

1119
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:39,220
we had when we first met.

1120
00:32:39,220 --> 00:32:40,040
When everyone felt like strangers.

1121
00:32:40,040 --> 00:32:40,760
That distance, right?

1122
00:32:40,760 --> 00:32:41,840
I think everyone really opened up.

1123
00:32:41,840 --> 00:32:43,520
It helped me understand Sun Bohan and Si

1124
00:32:43,520 --> 00:32:45,640
a lot better.

1125
00:32:49,450 --> 00:32:50,240
I'm in a pretty good mood.

1126
00:32:50,240 --> 00:32:51,760
I'm really happy.

1127
00:32:51,760 --> 00:32:53,070
I'll tell you tonight.

1128
00:32:54,720 --> 00:32:56,280
Wait, why do I look so gloomy?

1129
00:32:56,280 --> 00:32:56,920
Why?

1130
00:32:59,030 --> 00:33:00,010
He didn't get to ask Sha Yue'er out.

1131
00:33:00,010 --> 00:33:00,930
He's still disappointed.

1132
00:33:03,200 --> 00:33:04,160
He's replaying it all in his head.

1133
00:33:04,650 --> 00:33:05,850
Chen Hewen's actually still a little

1134
00:33:05,850 --> 00:33:06,780
worried about Sha Yue'er.

1135
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:08,800
I really was waiting for her then.

1136
00:33:10,420 --> 00:33:11,550
I think for girls,

1137
00:33:11,550 --> 00:33:12,420
the problem is,

1138
00:33:12,670 --> 00:33:13,730
if you go quiet for one night,

1139
00:33:13,730 --> 00:33:15,420
it already feels
like the world's ending.

1140
00:33:15,420 --> 00:33:15,710
Yeah!

1141
00:33:15,710 --> 00:33:16,110
A whole drama

1142
00:33:16,110 --> 00:33:16,790
plays out in your head.

1143
00:33:16,790 --> 00:33:17,420
Yeah.

1144
00:33:17,560 --> 00:33:18,400
Exactly!

1145
00:33:18,400 --> 00:33:19,200
(She gets me)

1146
00:33:19,200 --> 00:33:21,080
Yang Chaoyue was rooting for me earlier.

1147
00:33:21,080 --> 00:33:23,600
How'd everything fall apart already?

1148
00:33:23,600 --> 00:33:25,520
No, when she was rooting for you,

1149
00:33:25,520 --> 00:33:26,760
not that much time had passed.

1150
00:33:26,760 --> 00:33:28,080
It's only been a day.

1151
00:33:28,080 --> 00:33:29,680
Mainly because you came back
and didn't talk to me.

1152
00:33:29,680 --> 00:33:30,680
I didn't think

1153
00:33:30,680 --> 00:33:31,160
about that.

1154
00:33:31,160 --> 00:33:33,160
And the Signal messages every night.

1155
00:33:33,160 --> 00:33:34,940
(No text either)
Yeah, you didn't text me.

1156
00:33:34,940 --> 00:33:35,680
You didn't text me either.

1157
00:33:35,750 --> 00:33:36,180
But...

1158
00:33:36,180 --> 00:33:37,320
Why should I text you?

1159
00:33:37,360 --> 00:33:38,840
You didn't even invite me into your car.

1160
00:33:38,840 --> 00:33:39,200
Why would I?

1161
00:33:39,200 --> 00:33:40,600
How was I supposed to invite you?

1162
00:33:40,600 --> 00:33:41,640
How was I supposed to know you...

1163
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:42,480
I couldn't invite you.

1164
00:33:42,480 --> 00:33:44,120
How about I sit here
and let you two argue?

1165
00:33:45,160 --> 00:33:45,560
We're not arguing.

1166
00:33:47,120 --> 00:33:48,200
But I couldn't invite you.

1167
00:33:48,200 --> 00:33:49,040
You saw it yourself.

1168
00:33:53,640 --> 00:33:54,560
That toss right there.

1169
00:33:54,920 --> 00:33:56,280
That was a pretty good toss.

1170
00:33:56,540 --> 00:33:57,850
I've got goosebumps!

1171
00:34:07,440 --> 00:34:08,719
Looks so cool.

1172
00:34:10,800 --> 00:34:12,210
This is the stargazing room.

1173
00:34:12,210 --> 00:34:13,620
Nice.

1174
00:34:13,620 --> 00:34:14,699
(Can't hold back)
Nice.

1175
00:34:14,699 --> 00:34:15,170
Chen Hewen

1176
00:34:15,170 --> 00:34:16,320
has serious

1177
00:34:16,320 --> 00:34:17,340
guts.

1178
00:34:20,920 --> 00:34:22,440
Chen Hewen, back then,

1179
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:25,040
you were the first person
to open the stargazing room.

1180
00:34:25,040 --> 00:34:27,560
What was going through your mind?

1181
00:34:28,360 --> 00:34:29,840
I figured opportunities,

1182
00:34:29,840 --> 00:34:31,239
you know, go to those who are ready.

1183
00:34:32,159 --> 00:34:33,400
I don't like letting things drag on.

1184
00:34:33,400 --> 00:34:34,880
And I don't want anyone feeling awkward.

1185
00:34:34,880 --> 00:34:36,679
If there's something
between us, we should at least

1186
00:34:36,679 --> 00:34:38,440
put it out there and talk about it.

1187
00:34:38,440 --> 00:34:39,400
We just got here.

1188
00:34:39,400 --> 00:34:40,280
I don't want misunderstandings already.

1189
00:34:40,280 --> 00:34:41,280
Otherwise, I think

1190
00:34:41,280 --> 00:34:42,920
as we spend more time together,

1191
00:34:42,920 --> 00:34:45,760
it could make things awkward between us.

1192
00:34:45,760 --> 00:34:47,800
So I'll be the one
to open the stargazing room.

1193
00:34:50,889 --> 00:34:52,389
This is so dreamy.

1194
00:34:53,510 --> 00:34:54,590
She's not here?

1195
00:34:55,010 --> 00:34:55,770
He's still looking for Sha Yue'er.

1196
00:34:55,800 --> 00:34:57,880
Don't tell me you two
run into each other here.

1197
00:34:58,960 --> 00:34:59,800
We actually did.

1198
00:34:59,840 --> 00:35:01,050
I went back downstairs later.

1199
00:35:01,280 --> 00:35:02,440
A fateful encounter.

1200
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:07,640
This was when I was most nervous.

1201
00:35:07,640 --> 00:35:08,960
I was so nervous then.

1202
00:35:09,590 --> 00:35:10,490
Stargazing room invitation card.

1203
00:35:24,170 --> 00:35:25,370
Nice.

1204
00:35:25,660 --> 00:35:27,660
(Takes the invitation card)
Thanks.

1205
00:35:27,820 --> 00:35:28,740
(First stargazing room date invitation)

1206
00:35:28,990 --> 00:35:30,000
That day,

1207
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:31,280
I used three words to describe you.

1208
00:35:32,020 --> 00:35:33,280
You knew I meant you, right?

1209
00:35:34,020 --> 00:35:35,210
I knew.

1210
00:35:37,210 --> 00:35:38,020
From my perspective,

1211
00:35:38,020 --> 00:35:38,670
I've always thought

1212
00:35:38,670 --> 00:35:39,750
you have a really pretty smile.

1213
00:35:41,160 --> 00:35:41,840
Back then,

1214
00:35:41,840 --> 00:35:42,660
your eyes were like...

1215
00:35:42,660 --> 00:35:43,650
I can't imitate it,

1216
00:35:43,650 --> 00:35:44,360
but they were

1217
00:35:44,360 --> 00:35:45,260
like little crescent moons.

1218
00:35:46,480 --> 00:35:47,360
All curved.

1219
00:35:47,540 --> 00:35:48,320
Is that

1220
00:35:48,930 --> 00:35:49,970
you blushing, or

1221
00:35:49,970 --> 00:35:50,850
is that your makeup?

1222
00:35:52,350 --> 00:35:53,260
How would I know?

1223
00:35:53,260 --> 00:35:54,470
I can't see myself.

1224
00:35:56,100 --> 00:35:57,140
I think I'm blushing too.

1225
00:35:57,140 --> 00:35:58,840
Give me a second.

1226
00:35:59,680 --> 00:36:01,280
That's a lot to take in, huh?

1227
00:36:03,900 --> 00:36:04,950
At the dinner that night,

1228
00:36:05,860 --> 00:36:06,580
I actually

1229
00:36:06,580 --> 00:36:07,900
thought you were pretty brave.

1230
00:36:08,480 --> 00:36:08,960
What if I

1231
00:36:08,960 --> 00:36:10,020
hadn't been brave enough
to grab your card

1232
00:36:10,020 --> 00:36:10,970
and someone else took it?

1233
00:36:10,970 --> 00:36:12,610
More than failing,

1234
00:36:12,610 --> 00:36:13,500
what I can't accept

1235
00:36:13,500 --> 00:36:14,140
is not being brave.

1236
00:36:14,140 --> 00:36:15,420
(I'd rather fail than not be brave)

1237
00:36:17,620 --> 00:36:18,250
I can accept

1238
00:36:18,250 --> 00:36:19,370
messing up.

1239
00:36:19,800 --> 00:36:20,730
But I have to try first.

1240
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:29,800
Let's ask the person herself.

1241
00:36:29,800 --> 00:36:31,360
How did you feel at the time?

1242
00:36:34,440 --> 00:36:35,600
For a moment just now,

1243
00:36:35,600 --> 00:36:36,800
I got pulled back...

1244
00:36:36,800 --> 00:36:37,800
Into how you felt then, right?

1245
00:36:37,800 --> 00:36:38,880
Yeah.

1246
00:36:38,880 --> 00:36:40,640
I probably looked really happy then,

1247
00:36:40,640 --> 00:36:43,080
but that night,
I was actually pretty scared.

1248
00:36:43,920 --> 00:36:44,960
Because I felt like

1249
00:36:45,800 --> 00:36:46,960
if someone

1250
00:36:46,960 --> 00:36:49,320
makes me this uncertain

1251
00:36:49,320 --> 00:36:50,540
when we've barely started getting
to know each other,

1252
00:36:50,540 --> 00:36:51,880
then maybe

1253
00:36:51,880 --> 00:36:54,360
I don't know what he'll do to me later.

1254
00:36:56,680 --> 00:36:58,440
But honestly, I'm more...

1255
00:36:58,440 --> 00:36:59,760
In real life, I'm probably

1256
00:37:00,760 --> 00:37:01,920
really conflicted.

1257
00:37:01,920 --> 00:37:03,400
But here in the house, I wondered

1258
00:37:03,400 --> 00:37:04,760
just how brave I could be.

1259
00:37:04,760 --> 00:37:06,160
So I pushed myself too.

1260
00:37:07,440 --> 00:37:08,880
Everyone here is brave.

1261
00:37:11,600 --> 00:37:12,210
Ask another one.

1262
00:37:12,210 --> 00:37:12,940
Let me hear it.

1263
00:37:12,940 --> 00:37:13,750
Like on the first day,

1264
00:37:13,750 --> 00:37:15,160
when we were in the same room,

1265
00:37:15,160 --> 00:37:15,530
I felt

1266
00:37:15,530 --> 00:37:16,850
like you barely even looked at me.

1267
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:26,000
This is probably your first time

1268
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:27,520
seeing this too, right?

1269
00:37:28,480 --> 00:37:30,220
Seriously, I didn't even know Zhao Xilun...

1270
00:37:30,220 --> 00:37:30,940
(Turns around)

1271
00:37:38,720 --> 00:37:39,960
He's gone numb.

1272
00:37:44,040 --> 00:37:45,400
He's going out?

1273
00:37:47,240 --> 00:37:48,400
He's coming to find you guys?

1274
00:37:52,100 --> 00:37:52,999
(Pushes the door open and leaves)
Zhao Xilun

1275
00:37:52,999 --> 00:37:54,360
is pretty bold too.

1276
00:37:56,620 --> 00:37:57,390
Have your favorite Set A.

1277
00:38:02,550 --> 00:38:03,250
Hello.

1278
00:38:04,200 --> 00:38:04,760
Hello.

1279
00:38:04,980 --> 00:38:05,620
Hello.

1280
00:38:06,850 --> 00:38:08,000
Hi. You're back.

1281
00:38:08,600 --> 00:38:09,120
This...

1282
00:38:09,120 --> 00:38:09,900
Wow!

1283
00:38:11,120 --> 00:38:12,920
This is too good!

1284
00:38:13,240 --> 00:38:14,680
Pause it! Pause right here!

1285
00:38:14,680 --> 00:38:15,320
Hello.

1286
00:38:15,320 --> 00:38:15,920
You're back.

1287
00:38:16,840 --> 00:38:17,800
We need a second to process this.

1288
00:38:17,800 --> 00:38:18,400
Let's process this first.

1289
00:38:18,400 --> 00:38:19,200
Process it.

1290
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:23,560
My mind's gone blank.

1291
00:38:25,520 --> 00:38:27,080
This is intense.

1292
00:38:27,080 --> 00:38:28,520
So when Zhao Xilun came down,

1293
00:38:29,320 --> 00:38:30,360
what were you thinking at the time?

1294
00:38:31,760 --> 00:38:32,200
I...

1295
00:38:34,440 --> 00:38:35,680
Honestly, back then,

1296
00:38:35,680 --> 00:38:38,640
I wasn't really sure

1297
00:38:38,640 --> 00:38:40,240
if he was interested

1298
00:38:40,240 --> 00:38:41,040
in me.

1299
00:38:41,040 --> 00:38:42,520
Yeah, because earlier that day,

1300
00:38:43,240 --> 00:38:44,920
you two had just made squishies together

1301
00:38:44,920 --> 00:38:46,720
and started getting
to know each other better.

1302
00:38:46,720 --> 00:38:47,680
Yeah.

1303
00:38:49,320 --> 00:38:51,240
I really admire

1304
00:38:51,240 --> 00:38:52,640
Chen Hewen and Zhao Xilun.

1305
00:38:54,240 --> 00:38:56,040
Some of the things they do

1306
00:38:56,040 --> 00:38:57,120
are honestly

1307
00:38:57,120 --> 00:38:58,400
things someone like me

1308
00:38:58,400 --> 00:38:59,080
just...

1309
00:38:59,080 --> 00:38:59,640
Couldn't do.

1310
00:38:59,640 --> 00:39:00,840
I just couldn't.

1311
00:39:00,840 --> 00:39:01,640
Same here.

1312
00:39:01,640 --> 00:39:03,000
Even if I liked someone

1313
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:04,440
right from the start or whatever,

1314
00:39:04,440 --> 00:39:06,200
I still couldn't do that.

1315
00:39:06,200 --> 00:39:07,400
Yeah, exactly.

1316
00:39:07,400 --> 00:39:09,000
I keep a lot of feelings to myself.

1317
00:39:09,120 --> 00:39:09,920
Yeah.

1318
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:11,880
Si, did you know about this?

1319
00:39:11,880 --> 00:39:12,600
I had no idea.

1320
00:39:12,600 --> 00:39:13,840
I had zero perspective on it.

1321
00:39:13,840 --> 00:39:16,040
You really can't see what happens
outside your bubble.

1322
00:39:16,680 --> 00:39:18,640
How long has it been
since you left the house?

1323
00:39:19,040 --> 00:39:20,080
Do you miss

1324
00:39:20,080 --> 00:39:21,160
that time?

1325
00:39:21,160 --> 00:39:21,880
Yeah.

1326
00:39:21,880 --> 00:39:24,000
Yeah. It suddenly feels so long ago.

1327
00:39:24,000 --> 00:39:25,440
Watching this just took me right back.

1328
00:39:25,440 --> 00:39:26,040
It feels...

1329
00:39:26,040 --> 00:39:27,680
Like it was all a dream.

1330
00:39:29,360 --> 00:39:30,640
That's how we felt too.

1331
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:33,520
It's pretty amazing.

1332
00:39:33,520 --> 00:39:35,320
Watching this back makes you realize

1333
00:39:35,720 --> 00:39:38,160
you only saw your side of things then.

1334
00:39:38,160 --> 00:39:40,000
But now you get to see

1335
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:41,400
(So much)
how much everyone else was doing too.

1336
00:39:41,400 --> 00:39:42,720
Yeah, at the exact same time.

1337
00:39:42,720 --> 00:39:43,560
We felt that too.

1338
00:39:43,560 --> 00:39:45,600
Yeah. Everyone
had their own story going on.

1339
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:49,320
Si, after watching all this today,

1340
00:39:49,320 --> 00:39:52,680
and seeing yourself
and the house from another angle,

1341
00:39:52,680 --> 00:39:55,200
is there anything you want
to say to everyone?

1342
00:39:55,200 --> 00:39:56,800
Or anything you'd say to yourself?

1343
00:40:00,240 --> 00:40:01,840
First, when I watch myself,

1344
00:40:01,840 --> 00:40:03,400
I notice these little habits.

1345
00:40:03,760 --> 00:40:05,480
Like sometimes my head stays still,

1346
00:40:05,480 --> 00:40:06,480
but my eyes move around.

1347
00:40:06,480 --> 00:40:08,160
I never noticed that before.

1348
00:40:08,160 --> 00:40:09,160
Sometimes I think

1349
00:40:09,160 --> 00:40:10,400
it doesn't look that great.

1350
00:40:10,400 --> 00:40:11,920
So it's something useful
for me to notice.

1351
00:40:11,920 --> 00:40:14,800
I can work on changing it.

1352
00:40:14,800 --> 00:40:17,040
And watching everyone else,

1353
00:40:17,040 --> 00:40:19,080
I feel like everyone expresses
themselves differently.

1354
00:40:19,080 --> 00:40:19,920
And everyone's brave.

1355
00:40:19,920 --> 00:40:22,000
I want to move in that direction too

1356
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:23,560
and slowly become better.

1357
00:40:24,800 --> 00:40:25,640
I feel the same.

1358
00:40:25,640 --> 00:40:27,360
I can see some things about myself

1359
00:40:27,360 --> 00:40:28,520
that I should work on.

1360
00:40:28,520 --> 00:40:31,800
And I also get
to see the bigger picture.

1361
00:40:32,640 --> 00:40:34,000
I think that's pretty helpful.

1362
00:40:34,000 --> 00:40:36,880
Next time, I shouldn't
overthink so much.

1363
00:40:39,720 --> 00:40:40,920
Actually, before coming here,

1364
00:40:40,920 --> 00:40:43,240
I kept telling myself,

1365
00:40:43,240 --> 00:40:45,800
since I chose to come
to the Signal House,

1366
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:48,920
at the very least, I hoped

1367
00:40:48,920 --> 00:40:50,520
that when I looked back at myself,

1368
00:40:50,520 --> 00:40:51,520
I'd feel

1369
00:40:52,000 --> 00:40:53,360
like I was brave.

1370
00:40:55,680 --> 00:40:56,440
It's the same for all of us.

1371
00:40:56,440 --> 00:40:58,440
This whole experience is pretty special.

1372
00:40:58,720 --> 00:40:59,280
Yeah.

1373
00:40:59,840 --> 00:41:01,440
Seeing Zhao Xilun,

1374
00:41:01,440 --> 00:41:02,280
Chen Hewen,

1375
00:41:02,280 --> 00:41:03,440
the things they do,

1376
00:41:03,440 --> 00:41:05,840
and the good parts
of their personalities,

1377
00:41:06,320 --> 00:41:08,120
there's a lot I can learn from them.

1378
00:41:08,880 --> 00:41:11,360
Because there are a lot
of things I can't do myself.

1379
00:41:12,840 --> 00:41:13,680
But I think

1380
00:41:13,680 --> 00:41:15,160
different people
have different personalities.

1381
00:41:15,160 --> 00:41:16,280
Every approach and every relationship

1382
00:41:16,280 --> 00:41:17,720
has its own way of working.

1383
00:41:18,280 --> 00:41:19,440
Yeah, so I think, Sun Bohan,

1384
00:41:19,440 --> 00:41:21,760
you don't have to think that,
I can't do what they do,

1385
00:41:21,760 --> 00:41:23,400
so that means something about me.

1386
00:41:26,120 --> 00:41:27,760
If I were watching myself this season,

1387
00:41:27,760 --> 00:41:29,680
I don't think I could be like you guys

1388
00:41:29,680 --> 00:41:33,400
and talk openly
about my experiences

1389
00:41:33,400 --> 00:41:37,120
or be this honest
about what I was going through.

1390
00:41:37,120 --> 00:41:38,160
I think you're all really brave.

1391
00:41:38,160 --> 00:41:40,520
(Amazing)
So I think you're all amazing.

1392
00:41:40,960 --> 00:41:41,760
Thank you.

1393
00:41:45,040 --> 00:41:47,120
Now, give us a few words

1394
00:41:47,120 --> 00:41:48,600
to tease what's coming next.

1395
00:41:54,680 --> 00:41:55,920
I've got one.

1396
00:41:57,920 --> 00:42:00,360
Suddenly, a comet falls from the sky

1397
00:42:00,360 --> 00:42:02,720
(Comet)
and "crashes" into the house.

1398
00:42:06,640 --> 00:42:07,560
Who does it "hit"?

1399
00:42:12,360 --> 00:42:13,680
I'll use one word.

1400
00:42:13,680 --> 00:42:14,320
Okay.

1401
00:42:14,320 --> 00:42:15,480
Twists.

1402
00:42:17,680 --> 00:42:18,240
(Curious)
Now I'm curious.

1403
00:42:18,240 --> 00:42:20,160
(Curious)
Me too.

1404
00:42:21,760 --> 00:42:22,840
My turn.

1405
00:42:22,840 --> 00:42:26,360
The second round of dates gets exciting.

1406
00:42:26,360 --> 00:42:27,040
Really exciting.

1407
00:42:27,040 --> 00:42:28,720
Sounds exciting already.

1408
00:42:29,600 --> 00:42:31,640
The calm before the storm.

1409
00:42:32,840 --> 00:42:34,280
Are you talking about me?

1410
00:42:34,280 --> 00:42:35,360
Yeah, the two of us.

1411
00:42:38,320 --> 00:42:39,000
